======================================================================
DETAILED DRIFT ANALYSIS & EXPLANATION
======================================================================
🚨 CLINICAL PRACTICE SHIFT DETECTED
Between the training period (2014-2016) and the new data (2020-2022), patient treatment patterns have changed significantly.
The model will now trigger an adaptation phase to account for these shifts.

Key clinical changes driving this update:
• Urine Output Rate: Average value decreased from 0.52 to 0.38 (Severe Drift PSI: 0.22)
• Urine Output Ml Kg Hr Rate: Average value decreased from 0.52 to 0.38 (Severe Drift PSI: 0.22)
• Total Crystalloid Ml: Average value decreased from 908.82 to 639.82 (Severe Drift PSI: 0.10)
• Lactate Time Delta Mean: Average value decreased from 2.24 to 2.11 (Severe Drift PSI: 0.07)
• Central Line: Usage dropped by 5.9% in the newer data.

  physio observed-value PSI: 51 features, 47 exceed their own train-era null (max PSI 0.303703, median 0.011868)
    exceeding: ['heart_rate', 'sbp_noninvasive', 'dbp_noninvasive', 'sbp_invasive', 'dbp_invasive', 'map_invasive', 'temperature_c', 'spo2']

  Spearman stability: 40 features, 780 pairs
    pairwise mean|Δρ| 0.016974 (train-era null p95 0.004848)   ← EXCEEDS null
    structure similarity 0.988449 (null p05 0.999124)
    label_vasopressor      mean|Δρ(feature,label)| 0.026864, 0 sign flips
    label_intubation       mean|Δρ(feature,label)| 0.029959, 0 sign flips
    Marginal PSI stability says NOTHING about these numbers. If the
    pairwise structure holds but outcome associations move, say so — the
    labels ARE treatment decisions, so that is the expected direction.
