======================================================================
SUMMARY & AUDIT LOG
======================================================================
🚨 CLINICAL PRACTICE SHIFT DETECTED
Between the training period (2014-2016) and the new data (2020-2022), patient treatment patterns have changed significantly.
To maintain accuracy safely, the model locked its physiological representation and exclusively updated its treatment and fusion layers. This restores accuracy by forcing the network to relearn the specific features that carry high predictive importance but suffered from severe real-world drift (most notably Gcs Verbal Rate and Urine Output Ml Kg Hr Rate).

Key clinical changes driving this update:
• Urine Output Rate: Average value decreased from 0.52 to 0.38 (Severe Drift PSI: 0.22)
• Urine Output Ml Kg Hr Rate: Average value decreased from 0.52 to 0.38 (Severe Drift PSI: 0.22)
• Total Crystalloid Ml: Average value decreased from 908.82 to 639.82 (Severe Drift PSI: 0.10)
• Lactate Time Delta Mean: Average value decreased from 2.24 to 2.11 (Severe Drift PSI: 0.07)
• Central Line: Usage dropped by 5.9% in the newer data.

What to check before writing this up:
  1. acc_vs_bwt.png — Run B should sit up and to the RIGHT of C and C_l2sp:
     comparable ACC, BWT closer to zero. That is the two-stream claim in one
     figure. If C_l2sp matches B, the effect is regularization, not structure.
  2. retention_trajectory_*.png — after an era's own adaptation step, a flat
     line means no forgetting and a falling line means forgetting. Run C should
     fall faster with each additional step; that compounding is the mechanism.
  3. B vs B_mirror in paired_contrasts.json, on the EARLIER eras. If the mirror
     ties B, freezing a large block is what helped and the decomposition claim
     does not hold — this is the control a reviewer will look for first.
  4. placebo_adaptation.json — the placebo ran at a boundary the detector called
     quiet. If its gain approaches the real gain, 'adaptation helps' is really
     'more data helps' and the drift framing is not carrying weight.
  5. incident_* columns everywhere — the incident AUROC is the headline number,
     not the overall one. Expect it substantially lower; that is the honest value.
  6. drift_detection_log.json → 'deployable'. If false, only the label-dependent
     oracle fired and the auto-detection claim has to be softened.

On gradual drift: multiple boundaries firing is a RESULT, not a problem. State
it plainly — 'drift in MIMIC-IV is continuous rather than a single event, so we
adapt sequentially' is a stronger and more honest framing than a single
changepoint, and it is why the sequential protocol is used here.
